---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="Who we are and why we publish. Research Lab USA writes practical articles and laboratory notes for technical readers."
>
	<section class="rl-section rl-section--tight">
		<div class="rl-container">
			<div class="rl-section-head">
				<p class="rl-eyebrow">About</p>
				<h1>About Research Lab USA</h1>
				<p class="rl-lede">
					We publish the kind of writing we wanted to find ourselves: clear,
					specific, and honest about what is uncertain.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="rl-prose">
				<h2>Why we publish</h2>
				<p>
					A great deal of technical writing online is either too shallow to act
					on or written to rank rather than to inform. We started publishing to
					fill the gap in the middle — pieces detailed enough to be useful,
					written plainly enough to be read.
				</p>

				<h2>How we write</h2>
				<p>
					Every article states what we did, what we observed, and what remains
					unresolved. Where we are drawing on someone else's work, we say so
					and link to it. Where we are uncertain, we say that too, rather than
					rounding an open question up to a confident answer.
				</p>
				<p>
					We correct things publicly. When an article turns out to be wrong, it
					is updated with a note describing what changed and why, rather than
					quietly edited.
				</p>

				<h2>Who we are</h2>
				<p>
					[Write two or three sentences here about your team, background and
					location. Readers trust specifics far more than adjectives, so
					mention what you actually do and where you do it.]
				</p>

				<h2>Get in touch</h2>
				<p>
					Corrections, questions and article suggestions are all welcome —
					reach us through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> or by email
					at <a href="mailto:hello@researchlabusa.com">hello@researchlabusa.com</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
